# Rust build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Persistent state: databases, mail spools, TLS keys and certificates, backups.
# Deleting this loses the deployment — it is what the backups are for.
data/

# ...except the one `data/` that is source rather than state. The public suffix
# list is `include_str!`d into `selfhost-config`, so a clone without it does not
# compile — and until 2026-08-11 no clone had it: the rule above swallowed a
# build input, every fresh checkout failed at `crates/foundation/config/src/psl.rs`,
# and the production box only built because somebody had copied the file across by
# hand.
!crates/foundation/config/data/
!crates/foundation/config/data/public_suffix_list.dat

# Generated artifacts, rebuilt by `selfhost render`.
runtime/

# Secrets. Only .env.example is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# The live config carries hostnames and mailbox addresses.
selfhost.config.toml

# Site content served by the proxy — the user's websites, not this project's
# source. The one exception: sites/console is the web admin console's own SPA,
# shipped with the project, so it stays tracked.
sites/*
!sites/console/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Tool caches: the dx document index and the Helpers project index. Both are
# rebuilt from the tree they describe, so committing them only stores staleness.
.doc/
.helpers/

# ...except the one file under .doc/ that is source rather than cache — the same
# mistake, and the same correction, as crates/config/data above.
#
# A `.dx` file in the tree is a 71-byte pointer (`~ dx1 <sha256>`); the document's
# actual text lives content-addressed in this pack. Ignoring it meant every clone
# of this repository — including the production box — got fourteen dangling
# pointers and no documentation at all, while this Mac was the only machine where
# the project's maps existed. That is not hypothetical: `crates/rui/rui.dx` still
# carries a `rui-restored` block recording the day a document's content was lost
# to a pack rewrite and had to be replayed by hand from a session record.
#
# `index.db` genuinely is a cache (~7 MB, rebuilt from the pack and the tree), so
# it stays ignored. The pack does not rebuild from anything.
!.doc/
.doc/*
!.doc/repo.dxcp

# Scratch directory for the service-manager demo (see .demo/svc)
.demo/

# local agent/security notes — never commit. These two are *writing about* the
# defences: the guidebook's findings, the working notes, what is still weak and
# where. That is the half worth keeping off a public repository — unlike the
# scripts, which merely do standard hardening and say nothing a scan would not.
CLAUDE.md
docs/SECURITY.md

# Scratch deployments the dx labs build to prove a command works end to end.
# The lab rebuilds it on every run; nothing in it is source.
/gen/
